{
  "about": [
    "What detect.py knows. Edit this file to teach it a framework, test tool, database or CI service.",
    "frameworks: packages = its own package first, then packages that pull it in (pytest-django needs pytest).",
    "role = the forge profile it points to, 'server' (a server framework forge has no profile for),",
    "'static' (a front end) or 'test'. telltale = files that give it away when no manifest names it.",
    "telltale_words: such a file counts only when it holds the word (a Flask-Script manage.py is not Django).",
    "unless = leave it out when that one was found. Django's test runner (manage.py test) is built in, so it",
    "has no packages: its test files give it away, unless pytest was found (pytest runs those tests too).",
    "ecosystems: the language, the forge profile in that language, and file names in that language.",
    "databases: words in an image, package or setting that point to a database.",
    "ci_files: the file each CI service reads, from the top folder (inventory.py has the same table).",
    "container_files, python_manifests, database_files: file names; a pattern with a / fits the end of the path."
  ],
  "frameworks": [
